{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3747548af2df89d0d1419b39b254d552d070e58712717ae65893d9b4d81c6c0a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent uses Docker to provide a consistent, isolated execution environment, creating a Dockerfile when one does not exist in the target repository."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ae8bd61db604055d123b89321f208e6e6f53e929137c30ff73fd40af3057464"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Deployment is driven by a structured LangGraph workflow covering clone, file extraction, setup planning, command execution, error checking, and error fixing steps."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3e4135f377cacfe978ac85958ce7dde1211c99677167a74ef8c7c1840062a5ee"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The entry point is a Python script: running 'python main.py' deploys the repository whose URL is set in the github_repo_url variable in main.py."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3fad31d43f1e596cf81f8bd89e8475f4c3632fc97c2821289f0b7b5fc7618dab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The workflow includes an error-check step where an LLM analyzes terminal output after command execution, and a fix step that may modify the Dockerfile or commands and re-execute them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_41d18c70e02adaf81678dd104ec88154575725b7276a7fa54fbd3ec7ba92b01c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README notes the agent is not perfect and may encounter issues with certain repositories, recommending users review terminal output for errors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44ff88ceb5495fa9b8236d32c6c54c66da4d04af1ef67eb5a62f3871eba66ce5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The docker run command is prefixed with 'alacritty -e' to open a new terminal window, so the alacritty terminal must be installed on the user's machine."},{"claim_ids":["clm_73b179eb63235b1ced60889d5639b43bfa70eeb982461d65a5f87d621769e205"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The LLM is gpt-4o-mini by default, configurable in instantrun.py, and all LLM interactions follow a strict JSON output format for consistent parsing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7528710a3a1835c90ad3ae04b1bdd545788679c51d0ba1626aec74f2d8a1a93b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is described as an AI agent that autonomously deploys GitHub repositories on a user's local machine, handling cloning through command execution in Docker."},{"claim_ids":["clm_851213cbfee4bf33a95c5037c21dc697a3f4a4ba890ebf8b3cbf1f90565e0691"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: setup requires installing Python 3.10+, Docker, and pip packages, and setting an OpenAI API key and base URL directly in instantrun.py."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f74c45ba99c329b85b81575702271bb1256372c3eb1907c8aef43d68db3a0788"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is designed for Arch Linux but may be adaptable to other Linux distributions with minor modifications; it targets Python 3.10+ for Python projects."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f8e4405a94257d77eead51a58deb8ebdd662cb7934f85cb92b0e2977f59ab356"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"No benchmark or success-rate evaluation harness appears in the evidence; the only performance indications are two YouTube demo videos of deployments."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3747548af2df89d0d1419b39b254d552d070e58712717ae65893d9b4d81c6c0a","clm_3ae8bd61db604055d123b89321f208e6e6f53e929137c30ff73fd40af3057464","clm_3e4135f377cacfe978ac85958ce7dde1211c99677167a74ef8c7c1840062a5ee","clm_3fad31d43f1e596cf81f8bd89e8475f4c3632fc97c2821289f0b7b5fc7618dab","clm_41d18c70e02adaf81678dd104ec88154575725b7276a7fa54fbd3ec7ba92b01c","clm_44ff88ceb5495fa9b8236d32c6c54c66da4d04af1ef67eb5a62f3871eba66ce5","clm_73b179eb63235b1ced60889d5639b43bfa70eeb982461d65a5f87d621769e205","clm_7528710a3a1835c90ad3ae04b1bdd545788679c51d0ba1626aec74f2d8a1a93b","clm_851213cbfee4bf33a95c5037c21dc697a3f4a4ba890ebf8b3cbf1f90565e0691","clm_f74c45ba99c329b85b81575702271bb1256372c3eb1907c8aef43d68db3a0788","clm_f8e4405a94257d77eead51a58deb8ebdd662cb7934f85cb92b0e2977f59ab356"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:17:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb27438f7951401a9a6a632d123d4002","id":"